\begin{definition}
\label{def:6.20}
[Regular level set as a local graph]
Let $f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}$ be continuously differentiable, and let $x_0=(x_{0,1},\dots,x_{0,n}) \in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfy $f(x_0)=0$. If there exists an index $j\in\{1,\dots,n\}$ such that $\partial f/\partial x_j (x_0) \neq 0$, then there exist open sets $U\subset \mathbb{R}^{n-1}$ and $W\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ with $x_0\in W$, and a differentiable function $g:U\to\mathbb{R}$ such that
